Match Wine 10 MCIAVI's final-draw and audio-drain polling behavior.

MCIAVI_player exits the video loop as soon as its last permitted frame is
painted; it does not wait for the next video deadline. It tests outstanding
WaveOut headers immediately and sleeps 100 ms before each incomplete retry.
A real MCI fixture retaining two original Cinepak packets and one complete
ADPCM block plays only frame 0 and takes about 100 ms with a real-time virtual
ALSA device. The pre-fix port finishes at 46 ms and polls at every millisecond;
with no audio it incorrectly waits another 40 ms after the last image.

Preserve video/source PCM bytes and explicit cancellation. This fixes MCI
transport timing; WaveOut/SDL/WebAudio buffer completion, driver silence tails
and full original/live-port A/V timing remain separate acceptance requirements.

https://github.com/wine-mirror/wine/blob/wine-10.0/dlls/mciavi32/mciavi.c

